{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "ms-ml-private-inference-promotion-v1",
  "title": "Private machine-learning inference with controlled model promotion",
  "subtitle": "A separated Dev, Stage, and Prod architecture trains candidate models, promotes versioned artifacts, and serves online inference privately. Synthetic Azure reference; no deployment is implied.",
  "description": "### Problem\nEnterprise ML teams need a controlled path from experimentation to production inference, with environment isolation, private access, and traceable model artifacts.\n\n### Flow and Azure mapping\nA Dev environment reads governed training data, runs feature preparation and training, evaluates a candidate, and publishes approved model and environment versions to a shared Azure Machine Learning registry. Promotion pipelines import the approved artifacts into Stage and Prod. AKS hosts online endpoints behind Application Gateway and API Management; private endpoints, managed identities, and monitoring support operations. Blue/green deployment shifts traffic only after validation.\n\n### Trade-offs and assumptions\nThe Microsoft baseline is explicitly single-region and focuses on online inference; streaming inference is out of scope. The diagram should not imply that batch scoring, high availability, a particular feature store, or a full MLOps control framework is automatically included. Release gates and approval roles are conceptual, and must be designed for the organization's governance needs.\n\nSource: [Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/ai-ml/architecture/baseline-azure-machine-learning-inference).\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- Origin provider: Microsoft\n- Target: Azure conceptual adaptation\n- Primary source: [Baseline Azure Machine Learning Inference Reference Architecture](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/ai-ml/architecture/baseline-azure-machine-learning-inference)\n- Reviewed: 2026-11-06\n\n## Catalog status\n\nThis is an original, editable Azure conceptual adaptation. It is synthetic reference material, not a deployed system, certified vendor architecture, or automatic deployment plan.\n\n## Mapping caveats\n\n- Source architecture is single-region; a separate regional recovery design is required.",
